<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-acanthostega-gunnari-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Acanthostega gunnari Turing wavenumber at 105 µm (Famennian, 365 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 87.1/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 sets r = Dv/Du = 10 so the saturated FFT wavelength is 106.93 µm against analytic k_c = 104.9 µm (relative error 0.019). Dispersion Pearson r = 0.9999 and RMSE = 0.0050 on probe modes 10–20. Equal diffusion (r = 1) has max growth -0.0989. Tiktaalik (375 Ma) cross-ray growth is -0.621 (pattern off); its along-ray wavelength is 100.11 µm. Ichthyostega (363 Ma, Dv × 0.92) sits at 105.54 µm. Brussels skull foreground 0.557, coherency 0.527, circularity 0.330, orientation KS against the RD field 0.137. GIF 640×480, 12 frames; last frame is the fossil so the fitness crop has a real specimen target. Overall 87.1/100 (faithfulness 86.1, reproducibility 89.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit dff4f2b508d0d1939f865c2f90f7ffe070e890d6; environment: . Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 80, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 91, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 86, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/acanthostega_gunnari_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-acanthostega-gunnari-turing-wavelength-s0.py at dff4f2b508d0d1939f865c2f90f7ffe070e890d6, image/png, 557252 B, 1344×1008 px, artifact_sha256 ee8fcd1b8df7a3e38a0636214b811c779e4ffa426f93491dac3345b7dee8c2cc (sha256 ee8fcd1b8df7a3e38a0636214b811c779e4ffa426f93491dac3345b7dee8c2cc), spec_fingerprint c711774b8d595cd5a6f22703fc15b77247416d03dc05678953f2434b64d13ee2. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: c711774b8d595cd5a6f22703fc15b77247416d03dc05678953f2434b64d13ee2; artifact_sha256: ee8fcd1b8df7a3e38a0636214b811c779e4ffa426f93491dac3345b7dee8c2cc; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/acanthostega_gunnari_turing_wavelength_s0/acanthostega_gunnari_brussels_head_specimen.jpg=6eae655c40f0444c..., datasets/acanthostega_gunnari_turing_wavelength_s0/acanthostega_gunnari_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=dc929ab5cb065aa6...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-acanthostega-gunnari-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Acanthostega has eight digits and Ichthyostega seven (Coates & Clack 1990). | Tiktaalik has lepidotrichia and no digits (Daeschler, Shubin & Jenkins 2006). | Turing 1952 critical wavenumber; Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics; Murray 1981 wavelength selection. | Dermal ornament is present on the Acanthostega skull (Porro, Rayfield & Clack 2015) at a coarser scale than 105 µm.; reconstructed_in_script: Du = 110.73 µm²/time so analytic lambda_c = 104.9 µm at r = 10, a = 0.05, b = 1. | Fin-ray anisotropy alpha = 3.4 and Ichthyostega Dv factor 0.92. | One digit corridor reconstructed as 4200 µm (40 wavelengths).; transfer_boundary: The 105 µm target is the campaign primordium tier for this slot, applied with the Turing law, not a published melanosome measurement on MGUH or NHMD material.; does_not_claim: That fossil melanosomes of Acanthostega were measured at 105 µm. | That the Schnakenberg field is a pixel-wise reconstruction of the Brussels skull. The GIF terminus is the photograph; the ocellus panel is the model. | That alpha = 3.4 or the 0.92 factor is a caliper measurement.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: A second assessor from another provider has not scored this audit.",
        "remediation needed: No published Acanthostega melanosome spacing at 105 µm is available to replace the campaign scale.",
        "remediation needed: The 4.2 mm digit corridor, alpha = 3.4, and the Dv factor 0.92 remain reconstructions." ;
    pk:hasScore 8.71e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-acanthostega-gunnari-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Acanthostega gunnari Turing wavenumber at 105 µm (Famennian, 365 Ma) — Parameter expressivity: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Above onset, lambda(r) falls monotonically from r = 8 to r = 48. r = 1 is a negative control with sigma_max = -0.0989. Tiktaalik cross-ray (r_eff = 2.94) is inside the subcritical band; along-ray r_eff = 34 shortens lambda to 100.11 µm; Ichthyostega r = 9.2 lengthens it to 105.54 µm. Each knob moves the feature it is supposed to move." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
