<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-acanthostega-gunnari-turing-wavelength-s0> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Acanthostega gunnari Turing wavenumber at 105 µm (Famennian, 365 Ma) (Acanthostega gunnari)",
        "Acanthostega gunnari Turing wavenumber at 105 µm (Famennian, 365 Ma) faithfully reproduces Acanthostega gunnari morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-acanthostega-gunnari-turing-wavelength-s0-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-acanthostega-gunnari-turing-wavelength-s0-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-acanthostega-gunnari-turing-wavelength-s0-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-acanthostega-gunnari-turing-wavelength-s0-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/delphi10000-acanthostega-gunnari-turing-wavelength-s0-5> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) models/2026-delphi10000-acanthostega-gunnari-turing-wavelength-s0.py, morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_3102_acanthostega_gunnari_turing_wavelength_s0.lean implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Acanthostega gunnari specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is carried by the MorphoEval rubric assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-acanthostega-gunnari-turing-wavelength-s0.py>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_3102_acanthostega_gunnari_turing_wavelength_s0.lean> ;
    schema:about "Acanthostega gunnari" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: That alpha = 3.4 or the 0.92 factor is a caliper measurement.",
        "does_not_claim: That fossil melanosomes of Acanthostega were measured at 105 µm.",
        "does_not_claim: That the Schnakenberg field is a pixel-wise reconstruction of the Brussels skull. The GIF terminus is the photograph; the ocellus panel is the model.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Du = 110.73 µm²/time so analytic lambda_c = 104.9 µm at r = 10, a = 0.05, b = 1.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Fin-ray anisotropy alpha = 3.4 and Ichthyostega Dv factor 0.92.",
        "reconstructed_in_script: One digit corridor reconstructed as 4200 µm (40 wavelengths).",
        "reported_in_source: Acanthostega has eight digits and Ichthyostega seven (Coates & Clack 1990).",
        "reported_in_source: Dermal ornament is present on the Acanthostega skull (Porro, Rayfield & Clack 2015) at a coarser scale than 105 µm.",
        "reported_in_source: Tiktaalik has lepidotrichia and no digits (Daeschler, Shubin & Jenkins 2006).",
        "reported_in_source: Turing 1952 critical wavenumber; Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics; Murray 1981 wavelength selection.",
        "transfer_boundary: The 105 µm target is the campaign primordium tier for this slot, applied with the Turing law, not a published melanosome measurement on MGUH or NHMD material." ;
