    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/models/2026-delphi10000-acanthostega-gunnari-turing-wavelength-s0.py, https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/main/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_3102_acanthostega_gunnari_turing_wavelength_s0.lean; output: docs/media/acanthostega_gunnari_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png; organism: Acanthostega gunnari; environment: n/a; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Acanthostega has eight digits and Ichthyostega seven (Coates & Clack 1990). | Tiktaalik has lepidotrichia and no digits (Daeschler, Shubin & Jenkins 2006). | Turing 1952 critical wavenumber; Schnakenberg 1979 kinetics; Murray 1981 wavelength selection. | Dermal ornament is present on the Acanthostega skull (Porro, Rayfield & Clack 2015) at a coarser scale than 105 µm.; reconstructed_in_script: Du = 110.73 µm²/time so analytic lambda_c = 104.9 µm at r = 10, a = 0.05, b = 1. | Fin-ray anisotropy alpha = 3.4 and Ichthyostega Dv factor 0.92. | One digit corridor reconstructed as 4200 µm (40 wavelengths).; transfer_boundary: The 105 µm target is the campaign primordium tier for this slot, applied with the Turing law, not a published melanosome measurement on MGUH or NHMD material.; does_not_claim: That fossil melanosomes of Acanthostega were measured at 105 µm. | That the Schnakenberg field is a pixel-wise reconstruction of the Brussels skull. The GIF terminus is the photograph; the ocellus panel is the model. | That alpha = 3.4 or the 0.92 factor is a caliper measurement.]; phenomenon_size: 78 µm (7.82e-05 m, log10=-4.107 m, tier=4_cellular_10um); species_scale_ladder (10 runs from 78 µm to 17.6 cm): 78 µm:acanthostega-gunnari-bioelectric-polarity, 244 µm:acanthostega-gunnari-vertex-packing, 3.9 mm:acanthostega-gunnari-turing-wavelength, 7.8 mm:acanthostega-gunnari-clock-wavefront, 1.8 cm:acanthostega-gunnari-morphogen-condensation, 2.1 cm:acanthostega-gunnari-elastic-buckling, 2.4 cm:acanthostega-gunnari-flux-canalization, 3.4 cm:acanthostega-gunnari-branching-tree" ;
